   183	### 3.3 Authenticated release request and immutable candidate preparation
   184	
   185	`release-prepare.yml` triggers only on `issues: types: [opened]`. GitHub binds
   186	that event to the last protected-default-branch commit/ref and requires the
   187	workflow file on the default branch. There is no tag/push trigger,
   188	`repository_dispatch`, selectable-ref `workflow_dispatch`, or upstream
   189	workflow whose code or output becomes authority. The request issue uses one
   190	strict machine-readable template containing a unique request ID, intended
   191	semantic version, and candidate commit. Its title, body, issue number, sender,
   192	and every requested value are untrusted data.
   193	
   194	The external request client uses a short-lived, repository-scoped GitHub App
   195	installation token with exactly `Issues: write`; it creates the request through
   196	the GitHub issue endpoint. The App has no Contents, Actions, Workflows,
   197	Administration, Environments, Secrets, Checks, Deployments, or publication
   198	permission and is not a protected-branch or protected-tag ruleset bypass actor.
   199	The token is held outside repository Actions, is never copied into the issue or
   200	exposed to the workflow, calls only the issue-creation endpoint, and records the
   201	issue/audit receipt. Compromise can create, edit, close, reopen, label, or spam
   202	issues and comments allowed by that repository permission, including replayed
   203	or altered release requests; it cannot create/update/delete Git refs, GitHub
   204	Releases, or release assets, make an unprotected commit eligible, approve an
   205	environment, obtain production secrets, sign, or publish. Release owns
   206	initiation; recorded engineering/security/release approvals remain separate and
   207	mandatory at `release/review-gate`.
   208	
   209	The first job requires the expected repository, `issues/opened` event and issue
   210	template version, GitHub App installation/sender, unique issue and request IDs,
   211	`github.ref` equal to the protected default branch, and `github.workflow_sha`
   212	equal to the protected default-branch workflow revision whose file and policy
   213	SHA-256 digests are checked in. It parses only the event payload captured for
   214	that run, binds its digest, and never refetches a mutable issue body as
   215	authority. It then resolves the requested commit independently and requires it
   216	to be an exact commit reachable from the protected default branch.
   217	`release/revalidate` runs all nine checks fresh for that exact candidate.
   218	The intended `v*` tag must be absent and unreserved; it is created atomically at
   219	the accepted candidate commit only by the later protected publication job.
   220	Missing, replayed, ambiguous, moved, or inconsistent metadata is `unknown` and
   221	stops before candidate acceptance.
   222	
   223	Every credential-capable reusable workflow is called as
   224	`owner/repository/.github/workflows/<file>.yml@<full-reviewed-commit-SHA>` and
   225	that SHA plus file digest appears in the immutable candidate. Relative local
   226	workflow calls and tag/branch refs are prohibited for release authority because
   227	they resolve from mutable or caller-selected code.
   228	
   229	| Job / blocking check | Actor trust and input | Token / environment / secrets | Network | Outputs / retention | Approval |
   230	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   231	| `release/candidate-identity` | Default-branch `issues/opened` event; independently validate App sender, issue/template/request identity, immutable event-payload digest, and untrusted candidate SHA/version; require exact default-branch-reachable commit, absent intended tag, trusted workflow SHA, and policy digest | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets; external `Issues: write` request credential is unavailable to Actions | GitHub-hosted macOS public egress exists; only GitHub repository/ref/issue metadata reads are authorized | Immutable candidate manifest, issue/request identity, event digest, intended tag/version, commit ancestry, and workflow-provenance evidence; release-record/7y | Release-owner initiation; not release approval |
   232	| `release/revalidate` | Exact immutable candidate manifest and the nine checked-in required-check definitions at the accepted policy revision | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | GitHub-hosted macOS public egress exists; only immutable GitHub action/checkouts and checksum-pinned Mise, Tuist, Go, Syft, dependency, scanner, and advisory origins declared by the candidate are authorized; no production endpoint | Fresh result and digest for every active required check; release-record/7y | None |
   233	| `release/review-gate` | Exact candidate manifest plus complete fresh active evidence index and recorded approval identities | `contents: read`; no production environment; no secrets | GitHub-hosted macOS public egress exists; no network use is authorized after checkout/evidence retrieval | Machine verdict: promotable/non-promotable/unknown; release-record/7y | Recorded engineering/security/release approvals; human ratification remains `TASK-260717-2d308k` before publication |
   234	
   235	The candidate manifest records request identity, source commit, clean-state assertion, source and
   236	dependency locks, toolchain/SDK/runner images, protocol and relay manifests,
   237	marketing/build versions, intended absent tag, expected artifact names, the
   238	trusted caller workflow SHA/policy digest, every reusable-workflow SHA/file
   239	digest, and every evidence digest. It is immutable after
   240	`release/review-gate` starts.
