   289	## 4. Required-check and branch-protection policy
   290	
   291	The protected default branch and merge queue require the following exact check
   292	names. A skipped, cancelled, timed-out, neutral, stale, missing, or unknown
   293	result is non-success and blocks merge. Administrators and bots do not bypass
   294	the rule; emergency changes use the separately audited exception process and
   295	must restore all checks before release eligibility.
   296	
   297	1. `policy/github-actions`
   298	2. `policy/board-spec`
   299	3. `policy/version-release-metadata`
   300	4. `build/workspace-legacy`
   301	5. `test/core-protocol`
   302	6. `build/apple-credential-free`
   303	7. `build/relay-four-target`
   304	8. `security/supply-chain`
   305	9. `security/ci-threat-model`
   306	
   307	Checks are accepted only for the exact current pull-request head SHA. A base
   308	update, force-push, merge-queue synthetic commit, workflow-policy change, or
   309	dependency-lock change invalidates stale results. Branch protection must reject
   310	ambiguous duplicate check names from different workflows/apps. Release
   311	promotion additionally requires the three `release-prepare` checks and the
   312	applicable protected release receipts; PR checks alone never authorize release.
